# The calculus, frozen: every body kind the signature ships is an instance
# of one of the five judgment forms docs/spec/soundness.md §5.1 declares.
#
# The forms are a chosen partition rather than a discovered necessity --
# scaling folds into preservation if one prefers four -- and the point of
# writing them down is the admission rule that comes with them. A new rule
# is data under entry, preservation, or scaling. A new transformation
# recipe is the one admitted reason to add a body kind, because a
# transformation carries the computational content of the theorem it
# mechanizes, and adding one is a specification event.
#
# This gate is what keeps that from being prose. The repository has made
# the same move twice before, for diagnostic allocation and for the `means`
# sentences: a rule nobody checks is a rule that drifts.

# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/judgment_forms.py \
# RUN:   %zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json | FileCheck %s

# CHECK: judgment forms: every body kind is an instance of a declared form
# CHECK-DAG: entry: 4
# CHECK-DAG: preservation: 2
# CHECK-DAG: scaling: 1
# CHECK-DAG: transformation: 3
# CHECK-DAG: cut: structural, no body kind
